      "MINTY: I’m sorry I’m going to leave you, Farewell, oh farewell; But I’ll meet you in the morning...\nMINTY & SLAVES: Farewell, oh farewell! I’ll meet you in the morning, I’m bound for the promised land! On the other side of Jordan, Bound for the promised la…",
      "HARRIET: Now I’m tellin’ you we cain’t.\nJANE: I don’t think I can go no further, Minty. Feel like we goin’ in circles.\nJUNYAH: Ain’t everybody strong like you, sister.\nHARRIET: Somebody tell you escapin’ slavery was easy?! If you strong enough to bear de lash, you strong enough to run from it!",
      "PHOEBE: Dey comin’. We gotta go!\nHARRIET: We cain’t go on dat way. There’s danger!",
      "HARRIET: Go down, Moses, way down in Egypt land Tell all the Pharaohs to...\nSLAVES: Let my people go!",
      "HARRIET: When Israel was in Egypt land Let my people go! Oppressed so hard they could not stand...\nSLAVES: Let my people go!"
    ]
